{"id":8194825,"docketId":65292607,"caseName":"Ex parte Botwinski","caseNameFull":"Ex parte John Botwinski","slug":"ex-parte-botwinski","docketNumber":"","dateFiled":"1942-01-05","dateArgued":null,"dateCertGranted":null,"year":1942,"scdbId":"","direction":"","votesMajority":null,"votesMinority":null,"disposition":"","posture":"","syllabus":null,"summary":null,"headnotes":null,"proceduralHistory":null,"attorneys":"Mr. Oscar B. Thiel for petitioner.","natureOfSuit":"","citationCount":10,"judges":"","jurisdictionType":"","opinions":[{"id":8156760,"type":"majority","typeCode":"020lead","perCuriam":false,"author":"","joinedBy":"","pageCount":null,"textLength":1351,"isHtml":true,"text":"<opinion type=\"majority\">\n<author id=\"A8rl\">\n<em>Per Curiam:</em>\n</author>\n<p id=\"AWFP\">It does not appear that petitioner has exhausted his state remedies by applying for a writ of error coram nobis. <em>State ex rel. Dowd </em>v. <em>Superior Court of La Porte County, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"3422617\"><a href=\"/opinion/3425619/state-ex-rel-dowd-v-superior-ct-of-laporte-co/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: State Ex Rel. Dowd v. Superior Ct. of Laporte Co.\">36 N. E. 2d 765</a></span>; <em>State ex rel. Kunkel </em>v. <em>Circuit Court of La Porte County, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"3425519\"><a href=\"/opinion/3428295/state-ex-rel-kunkel-v-laporte-circuit-court/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: State Ex Rel. Kunkel v. Laporte Circuit Court\">209 Ind. 682</a></span>, <span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"3425519\"><a href=\"/opinion/3428295/state-ex-rel-kunkel-v-laporte-circuit-court/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: State Ex Rel. Kunkel v. Laporte Circuit Court\">200 N. E. 614</a></span>. The motion for leave to file a petition for writ of habeas corpus is therefore denied without prejudice. <em>Mooney </em>v. <em>Holohan, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"102372\"><a href=\"/opinion/102372/mooney-v-holohan/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Mooney v. Holohan\">294 U. S. 103</a></span>.</p>\n</opinion>"}],"citations":[]}